7. Settlement and supply controls
- Rewards must come from reconciled, adequately funded reserves, not assumed new minting.
- A calculated preview is not an approved award; a submitted transaction is not proof of payment.
- Payout completion requires a successful on-chain receipt, matching token transfer, and reconciliation against an auditable award record.
- Double-payment protections must apply across seasons, bots, placements, retries, and transaction identifiers.
- Treasury changes, material allocation changes, and activation status should be disclosed through official channels.
8. Risks and policy status
TDIA is intended as a utility and rewards token, not as an equity interest, dividend right, guaranteed repurchase claim, or promise of appreciation. Digital tokens carry market, custody, liquidity, smart-contract, and operational risks. Depending on jurisdiction and design, token rewards and competitive promotions can implicate gaming, sweepstakes, tax, consumer, and financial laws; tailored review is required before activating transferable-token prizes.

Status as documented October 21, 2026: TDIA's token contract was previously deployed on Base mainnet; season payout features were not active; membership checkout was disabled. This repository document does not itself activate either feature or attest to current on-chain balances.

